From d8ebe5ac8e41e970837500dcfaed9c9e19813d57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:07:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ld: xfail pr24511 on MicroBlaze except Linux

pr24511.d xfails microblaze*-*-elf*, for the reason its comment gives:
ld/scripttempl/elfmicroblaze.sc defines neither __init_array_start nor
__fini_array_start.  Every MicroBlaze triplet except microblaze*-linux*
uses that script, so on microblaze-rtems the test fails rather than
xfails.

xfail microblaze*-*-* and add "#noxfail: microblaze*-linux*", the form
pr23658-1e.d uses for the same split.  microblaze*-linux* uses elf.sc,
which provides the symbols, so the test passes there; without the
#noxfail line it would XPASS.

ld/
	* testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d: xfail all MicroBlaze targets except
	microblaze*-linux*.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d b/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
index f77a43b9e2e..2b18a2e1c6d 100644
--- a/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
+++ b/ld/testsuite/ld-elf/pr24511.d
@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@
 # Most targets with their own scripts don't support init/fini_array and
 # thus don't define __init/fini_array_start.
 #xfail: avr-*-* cr16-*-* crx-*-* d10v-*-* d30v-*-* dlx-*-* ft32-*-* iq2000-*-*
-#xfail: m68hc1*-*-* mep-*-* microblaze*-*-elf* s12z-*-* v850-*-* visium-*-*
+#xfail: m68hc1*-*-* mep-*-* microblaze*-*-* s12z-*-* v850-*-* visium-*-*
 #xfail: xgate-*-* xstormy*-*-*
+#noxfail: microblaze*-linux*
 # Some targets with their own scripts haven't kept up with elf.sc and
 # PROVIDE __init_array_start rather than using PROVIDE_HIDDEN.  These
 # result in D symbols.  rx-elf makes .init/fini_array SHF_EXECINSTR so
